    {
      "name": "hx-disable",
      "description": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "value": "Meaning differs by version. htmx 2: disables htmx processing for the given node and any children nodes (htmx 4 spells this `hx-ignore`). htmx 4: adds `disabled` to the selected elements while a request is in flight (the htmx 2 `hx-disabled-elt` behaviour)."
      },
      "references": [
        {
          "name": "htmx Reference",
          "url": "https://htmx.org/attributes/hx-disable/"
        },
        {
          "name": "htmx 4 Reference",
          "url": "https://four.htmx.org/attributes/hx-disable/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "hx-disabled-elt",
      "description": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "value": "htmx 2 only. Removed in htmx 4: use `hx-disable`.\n\nadds the `disabled` attribute to the specified elements while a request is in flight"
      },
      "references": [
        {
          "name": "htmx Reference",
          "url": "https://htmx.org/attributes/hx-disabled-elt/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "hx-disinherit",
      "description": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "value": "htmx 2 only. Removed in htmx 4: inheritance is explicit in htmx 4 via the `:inherited` attribute suffix.\n\ncontrol and disable automatic attribute inheritance for child nodes"
      },
      "references": [
        {
          "name": "htmx Reference",
          "url": "https://htmx.org/attributes/hx-disinherit/"
